        <detaileddescription>
<para>Allocating constructor. Constructs a new message sink that sends messages to the syslog daemon. The syslog API doesn&apos;t use a handle to refer to the syslog, nor does it specify what happens when <computeroutput>openlog</computeroutput> is called more than once, or whether the <computeroutput>ident</computeroutput> string is copied. Best practice is to use only constant strings as the <computeroutput>ident</computeroutput> argument. </para>        </detaileddescription>
